.TH HAMANI_LOGANALYZER 1 "November 16, 2026" "Custom Shell Project" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hamani_loganalyzer \- analyze a log file using memory-mapped I/O
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamani_loganalyzer
.B -f
.I file
.br
.B hamani_loganalyzer
.B -h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hamani_loganalyzer
opens a regular log file for reading, checks its size with
.BR fstat (2),
and maps it into memory with
.BR mmap (2).
It counts the lines and puts each one under ERROR, WARNING, INFO, or OTHER.
Uppercase and lowercase both work. Only whole words match.
WARN and WARNING both count as warnings.
If a line has more than one level, ERROR comes first, then WARNING, then INFO.
Blank lines count as OTHER.
The last line still counts if it has no newline at the end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -f " file"
Pick the log file to read (required).
.TP
.B -h
Show the help message.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B hamani_loganalyzer -f hamani_loganalyzer_sample.log
.B hamani_loganalyzer -f "/path/to/server.log"
.B hamani_loganalyzer -h
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Prints the file name, total lines, Errors, Warnings, Info, and Other counts.
Each line goes into one group, so these counts add up to the total lines.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
File or system call error.
.TP
.B 2
Incorrect arguments.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT (Ctrl+C).
.TP
.B 143
Interrupted by SIGTERM.
.SH NOTES
The mapping is read-only. This command does not change the file.
Use a saved log file that stays the same while the command runs.
Shortening a file while it is mapped can cause SIGBUS.
If SIGINT or SIGTERM arrives while scanning, the command removes the mapping
and prints a cancellation message to standard error.
It does not print unfinished counts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmap (2),
.BR fstat (2),
.BR getopt (3),
.BR sigaction (2)
.SH AUTHOR
Operating System I Custom Shell group project.
